1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
A data-flow analysis is four answers, not a list of formulas.

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Direction is forward or backward; the domain is a lattice of facts.

3
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Meet combines two paths; the transfer function says what one block does.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Four subsets of two variables form a lattice under inclusion.

5
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:50,000
A may analysis meets with union; a must analysis meets with intersection.

6
00:00:50,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Turning the order round turns the empty set into the top element.

7
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:10,000
GEN is what a block makes true; KILL is what it makes false.

8
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:20,000
KILL means one thing for a definition, another for a variable, another for an expression.

9
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:30,000
OUT is GEN together with whatever came in and was not killed.

10
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:40,000
Forward: IN comes from predecessors, and the boundary is the entry.

11
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:50,000
Backward: swap IN and OUT, predecessors for successors, entry for exit.

12
00:01:50,000 --> 00:02:00,000
The equations are identical once you swap the names.

13
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:10,000
Start optimistic, then let the values fall to the truth.

14
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:20,000
On this four-block graph the values stop changing in two rounds.

15
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:30,000
It must stop: the lattice has finite height and the functions are monotone.

16
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:40,000
Four blocks, one back edge, and five variables.

17
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:50,000
USE and DEF come from the block; IN and OUT come from the neighbours.

18
00:02:50,000 --> 00:03:00,000
The exits are a, i, j; a, j; a, j; a, i, j — option D.

19
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:10,000
An expression is available if every path computes it and none destroys it.

20
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:20,000
Intersecting at the join says a + b is not available; union says it is.

21
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:30,000
Inside the left branch the expression is redundant; after the join it is not.

22
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:40,000
A reaching definition is an assignment, not a variable.

23
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:50,000
Forward, union, and a kill set of every other definition of the same variable.

24
00:03:50,000 --> 00:04:00,000
The entry of the join holds three definitions; a path search agrees.

25
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:10,000
A constant-propagation lattice has three kinds of value.

26
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:20,000
One branch sets x to one and y to two; the other swaps them.

27
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:30,000
Meet-over-all-paths gives three; the fixpoint gives not-a-constant.

28
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:40,000
Four analyses, four cells of one grid.

29
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:50,000
Union at a must-join, a forgotten back edge, a dropped GEN.

30
00:04:50,000 --> 00:05:00,000
Two answers per analysis: what it computes, and which optimisation it enables.

